-- title:
--   Integrality of Y⁶̂ j⁴(̂ j-1728)³ over ℂ[̂ j]
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$ and a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$. Write $\hat j =$ `coeffEmb ℂ jq` for the Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$ obtained from $\hat j_{\mathbb{Q}} = q^{-1}\cdot$ `jNumQ` $\in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ — the Hahn series `single (-1) 1` times the power series `jNum` with its integer coefficients pushed into $\mathbb{Q}$ — by applying the structure map $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$ to every coefficient; this is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Let $Y \in \mathbb{C}((q))$ be a Laurent series satisfying $Y \cdot \theta(\hat j) = \hat f$, where $\theta =$ `thetaL ℂ` is the $\mathbb{C}$-linear operator $g \mapsto q\, g'$ on $\mathbb{C}((q))$ (multiplication by `single 1 1` after the formal derivative of Laurent series), and where $\hat f$ denotes the $q$-expansion `qExpansion 1 f` of $f$, a power series over $\mathbb{C}$ regarded as an element of $\mathbb{C}((q))$. Then the Laurent series $$Y^6\,\hat j^{\,4}\,(\hat j - 1728)^3$$ is integral over the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by $\hat j$.
--
--   The series in question is the $q$-expansion of $f^6/\Delta$, a weight-zero meromorphic modular function for $\Gamma_0(N)$ holomorphic on the upper half-plane, whose integrality over $\mathbb{C}[j]$ is the standard mechanism identifying such functions with functions on the modular curve; the hypothesis $Y\cdot\theta\hat j = \hat f$ records that $Y$ is the $q$-expansion of the coefficient of $f$ against $dj$. It is used in establishing that a $q$-expansion of the stated shape comes from a regular differential, via [`ModularCurve.mem_regularDifferentialsBar_of_coeffMap_diffQExpBar_eq_qExpansion`](thm.html#ModularCurve.mem_regularDifferentialsBar_of_coeffMap_diffQExpBar_eq_qExpansion).
